 made 2026-08-10 for CIPH-39 (Windows Compatibility).\\n\\n## Issue\\n\\nPath arguments containing backslashes (Windows-style, e.g. `C:\\\\docs\\\\input.pdf`) were mishandled by the CLI's path parser, which had only been exercised against forward-slash paths on Linux/macOS.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-23\\n\\n# Windows Backslash Path Handling Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2023\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-19 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-10)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the path-handling fix made 2026-08-10 for CIPH-39 (Windows Compatibility).\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nPath arguments are now normalized to the platform-native separator before they reach the file-loading code, rather than assuming forward slashes everywhere.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-23\\n\\n# Windows Backslash Path Handling Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2023\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-19 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-10)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the path-handling fix made 2026-08-10 for CIPH-39 (Windows Compatibility).\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis note covers path-string handling only. It does not cover code signing or Windows Defender/SmartScreen behavior — those are separate, later concerns for CIPH-39 and are not addressed here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 23 window backslash path handl note owner evan document key doc 2023 last updat 2026 08 19 retrospect cover 2026 08 10 retrospect note on the path handl fix made 2026 08 10 for ciph 39 window compat issu path argument contain backslash window style e g c doc input pdf were mishandl by the cli s path parser which had onli been exercis against forward slash path on linux maco sourc id src gdoc 23 window backslash path handl note owner evan document key doc 2023 last updat 2026 08 19 retrospect cover 2026 08 10 retrospect note on the path handl fix made 2026 08 10 for ciph 39 window compat fix path argument are now normal to the platform nativ separ befor they reach the file load code ra